## Feature 2: Repo Relevance Validator

### The problem

`search_implementation` may return a repo that:
- Has the same topic area (e.g., "transformers") but implements a *different* paper
- Has the arXiv ID mentioned in a README comment but isn't actually the paper's code
- Is a popular framework that was returned due to keyword similarity

### Validation signals

| Signal | Score |
|---|---|
| arXiv ID found in repo README/description | +40 pts |
| Paper title (fuzzy match ≥ 80%) in README | +30 pts |
| Author names found in README/commits | +15 pts |
| Paper keywords density in README | +10 pts |
| Repo name contains paper acronym | +5 pts |
| **Threshold: < 30 pts → flag as "possibly irrelevant"** | |

