## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Docker availability**: The build test requires Docker to be installed and running locally. Should the build test be opt-in (run only when Docker is available, skip gracefully otherwise)?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Which sample paper to build?**: For the real `docker build` test, I plan to pick the sample paper that produces the *fewest Dockerfile validation issues* as the representative. Is this the right strategy, or should we always pick a specific one (e.g., BERT or LoRA)?

> [!NOTE]
> **Relevance threshold**: I set the "possibly irrelevant" threshold at 30/100. The score comes from: arXiv ID match (+40), title fuzzy match (+30), author names (+15), keyword density (+10), acronym match (+5). Let me know if you want to adjust.

> [!NOTE]
> **Docker Hub API**: Checking base image freshness uses the public Docker Hub API (no auth needed for public images). Known EOL tags (like `cuda:10.x`, `python:3.6`) are also hardcoded in a lookup table for offline fallback.

